HEAD is now at b899019 Tests re-read on pt-v20's graded arm, where each pinned the value or the behaviour pt-v20 had before it took the eighteen dials. The eight "off on every shipped preset" tests (buyback_yield_cap, cycle_publication_lag, fear_greed_published_inputs, gdp_publication_lag, macro_publication_repricing, fair_value_market_linear, unemployment_adjustment_half_life, fair_value_vix_discount) run on every preset through pt-v19, and a new test beside each holds pt-v20's value. The dial tests whose "off" arm was pt-v20 itself take pt-v20 with that dial at 0 (cycle and GDP lags' snapshot and hash tests and the GDP restore refusal; unemployment's contraction path, snapshot and restore refusal; the market-linear test with the market share at 0); the VIX-discount helper pins the knee at 30 and no smoothing, the values those tests were written on. The perturbation table (test_model_params) is re-measured on the new default, each with the replaced value in its comment: nine rows whose probe value was now pt-v20's own are re-valued (anticipation 63, rate sensitivity 4, the lags 126 and 42, unemployment 42, the fear and greed switch and the repricing back to 0, market-linear 0, the volatility ceiling 0.5); the earnings cycle's depth, upside and half-life and the anticipation are live through the repricing at publication (inert with it off, measured); the knee and half-life rows keep False with the reason restated; fed_liftoff_rule, qe_pe_gain, qe_pe_stock_gain and jump_momentum_share go inert and vix_return_clamp live, because the arm's burn-in at seed 42 opens the probe at fed funds 0.0 with QE inactive; oil_supply_response and oil_opec_symmetry rejoin ECONOMY_STREAM_MOVERS (+34 and -2 economy draws, the market stream unmoved). test_sampled_verification walks the economy's nested gdp_publication block field by field and knows pt-v20's four new conditional economy keys; the Python hash twin covers every one. test_scenario reads the packaged recession's true phase from the snapshot, since pt-v20 publishes it 252 sessions late. test_externality's pinned-VIX yield test stops at session 16, the last before the run's first meeting, which the arm's path brings forward to session 17. test_bonds: the rate shock's 2-year is re-measured (widening each session to the meeting at day 54, then re-anchored at -3.50 per cent), and the leak test's after-close half runs on pt-v19, with the before-close half checked on pt-v20. Three engine unit tests take pt-v19 where they needed a preset without the publication lags (the published phase and growth tests' off arms) or whose two phase ages draw differently (the macro-branch stream test). cargo test: 557 passed, 0 failed. pytest -n 4: 49 failed, 19 of them failing on the merge before any value was set (the LLM replays, pt-v20's record, callable five_days); the other 30 are not pinned values and are left failing for the owner (see the branch's report)
